<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul I of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1754">1754</a>–<a href="/years/1801">1801</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a>, reigned as emperor from 1796 to 1801. In 1799 he granted a monopoly charter to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-american-company">Russian-American Company</a> to govern Russian America, and in 1800 he decreed the annexation of the Georgian kingdom of Kartli-Kakheti, completed after his death. Erratic and autocratic, he was murdered by conspirators in 1801.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-i-of-russia.jpg" alt="Paul I of Russia" width="320" height="437" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vladimir Borovikovsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Paul_I_of_Russia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
